Description: avutil/tdrdi, avcodec/hevc: keep the whole mantissas of the displays
 .
 The mantissas of the reference display width and viewing distance are
 Max(0, exponent + prec - 31) bits long, up to 62 bits (H.265 V11
 G.14.3.3). The decoder reads them whole into HEVCSEITDRDI, but
 AV3DReferenceDisplay keeps them in uint8_t, so the frame side data
 carries only their low 8 bits.
 .
 Existing fields cannot change size, so add the whole mantissas as
 uint64_t at the end of AV3DReferenceDisplay (its size is not part of the
 ABI, see the structure's documentation), fill them in the HEVC decoder
 and pass them on in nvenc.
 .
